  "2026-10-25T01:35:24.638Z","harness:codex","Verification: the existing signal-store matrix now proves missing/stale/source/cursor/corpus/recency refreshes return rebuilt candidates without a stale warning. Corrupt snapshots and read/write failures retain recovery details, including a stale snapshot whose replacement write fails. The linked10-test run passes. A real repository context read returned no warnings and a current hosted pm.command span; the installation-scoped00:07-00:24UTC cohort had43 starts and43 finishes with no unmatched/orphan/duplicate sessions. Full static quality passes. The final canonical coverage run is still in progress and is not yet claimed as passed."
  "2026-10-25T01:49:07.849Z","harness:codex","Final pre-PR acceptance: Cursor/source/corpus/recency refresh and stale-write-failure controls pass; a live context read returned no warnings and a fresh hosted command span. Full canonical suite: 11227 passed, 3 skipped; exact source coverage100/100/100/100. Full static quality, typecheck, focused/linked PM tests and packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx acceptance pass. Hosted exact-head checks and external reviews remain required before merge; no publication claim is made by this source closure."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T00:57:50.438Z","harness:codex","A successful derived-cache refresh is ordinary maintenance, so report its cache_status and use the rebuilt data in the current response. Recovery warnings should identify a remaining storage/validation problem rather than instruct an agent to repeat a read that has already repaired itself."
